{**
 * c-spinner - a wait, said in words: a status naming what is being loaded, and
 * a turning shape beside the words for whoever can see it turn.
 *
 * The words are the component and the shape is its decoration, hidden from
 * assistive technology. A shape alone would tell somebody who cannot see it
 * nothing, and would tell somebody who asked for less motion nothing either
 * once it stopped turning - so for them the shape stands still and the words
 * are shown beside it (assets/base.css). Everybody else sees the shape turn and
 * has the words read out, unless labelShown asks for them on the page too.
 *
 * It is a status, so a screen reader says the words when the spinner appears
 * without the focus moving to it. The label is required: "loading" on its own
 * does not say what is being waited for.
 *
 * Two sizes, both the theme's: the default one for a region that is loading,
 * and the small one as tall as the text beside it, for a line or a button row.
 *}

{define spinner, string $label, string $size = 'default', bool $labelShown = false, ?string $testId = null}
    {do Trilobit\Core\Presentation\Component\Argument::oneOf('c-spinner', 'size', $size, ['default', 'small'])}

    <span
        n:class="'c-spinner', $size === 'small' ? 'c-spinner--small', $labelShown ? 'c-spinner--labelled'"
        role="status"
        data-testid="{$testId}"
    >
        <span class="c-spinner__shape" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="c-spinner__label">{$label}</span>
    </span>
{/define}
